ther  refused to let him sacrifice his  education and forced him to return to  hogwarts even though he himself was  immensely resentful of the duty that was  thrust upon him then he met gelat  grindelwald and was seduced into the  pursuit of the deathly hallows and a  vision of conquering muggles aberforth  was horrified before even though he was  a gruff peculiar young wizard he was  also a very decent person it would seem  that he never held any prejudice against  muggles despite what had happened to his  sister which meant that he thought a  plan to force them into servitude was  disturbing indeed he was also intensely  concerned for ariana's well-being if  albus was planning to travel the globe  and overthrow the entire mughal  population while also caring for their  sister she would clearly be in immense  danger and so aberforth bravely although  some may say foolishly confronted albus  and grindelwald this was the  confrontation which resulted in the  tragic death of ariana  despite this tragedy being the result of  a random curse the source of the spell  remaining a mystery even to this day  appleforth blamed albus for her death he  even punched albus in the face at  ariana's funeral breaking his nose and  signifying the end of their somewhat  already strained relationship as ab  fourth grew into adulthood he gained a  reputation as a wizard who was not a  people person  in fact in any disagreement he much  preferred to duel rather than debate and  he was known to occasionally fling goat  dung at those who opposed him in an  argument he was not particularly  interested in academics and he pursued a  lifelong career as the barkeep and  landlord of the hogshead inn in  hogsmeade the all-wizarding village  close to hogwarts in the gobber to fire  albus even suggested that aberforth may  have been illiterate although i think  this was simply albus's particular brand  of humor since we know that aberforth  attended hogwarts and therefore had had  an education  in 